        heading: "Redundancy architecture: double-ended substations",
        body: "The standard terminal power architecture is double-ended: two utility services (or two transformers from one service) feeding a main-tie-main switchgear lineup, so any single failure — utility outage, transformer fault, maintenance — leaves the building fully powered. The tie breaker logic (open or closed transition) is engineered, not assumed, and the sequence is tested during commissioning. For critical operations branches, the design may add a third source or UPS-backed distribution. Apex Grid sizes the services from the connected-load and demand calculations, then proves the redundancy in the one-line diagrams and the commissioning plan."
