        heading: "Wind design for doors in every position",
        body: "A hangar door must be engineered closed, open, and partially open — the partial positions often govern, because a half-open leaf catches wind the closed door sheds. ASCE 7 components-and-cladding pressures apply to the leaf and its guides, and the reactions go into the end-wall frame design. In hurricane and tornado regions, the door is frequently the building's weak link; the spec calls out the design wind speed and the missile-impact requirements where the code (e.g., Florida Building Code) demands them. Apex Grid includes the door positions as structural load cases, not as vendor-responsibility footnotes."
