        heading: "Verification, programs, and easements",
        body: "Sound-insulation programs — FAA-funded for eligible homes and schools, airport-funded for airport buildings — require verification: pre- and post-construction noise measurements proving the interior criterion is met. Avigation easements recorded against the property disclose the noise exposure permanently. For airport buildings, the commissioning includes acoustic testing of representative spaces. Apex Grid writes the verification protocol into the construction documents and coordinates the testing — because an acoustic design without verification is a promise, not a result."
